<title>CANADA: Canada October bankruptcies rise over year.</title>
<headline>Canada October bankruptcies rise over year.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bankruptcies in Canada rose to 8,851 in October from 7,559 a year earlier, the Department of Consumer and Corporate Affairs said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The department said 1,206 businesses and 7,645 consumers went bankrupt in the month.</p>
<p>In September, 7,632 bankruptcies were recorded.</p>
<p>For the year to date, 78,206 bankruptcies have been registered (12,034 businesses and 66,172 consumers), up from 65,088 in the same period last year.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau, 613-235-6745))</p>
